# Code owners for the protected-evidence surface.
#
# What this file does
# -------------------
# GitHub automatically requests a review from the listed owner whenever a pull
# request touches one of these paths, and surfaces a "code owner review" marker
# on the PR. That makes changes to protected evidence, its baselines, or the CI
# gate itself hard to merge without noticing them.
#
# What this file does NOT do
# --------------------------
# This is a single-maintainer repository. GitHub does not allow an author to
# approve their own pull request, so CODEOWNERS here cannot create independent
# authorization -- the sole owner would either self-merge with admin rights or
# bypass the requirement. Its value is review VISIBILITY, not separation of duty.
#
# Concretely: it does not stop the known limitation where protected text and its
# expected SHA-256 baseline are changed together in one commit. It only ensures
# such a change appears in a pull request that is flagged for owner review.

# Recruiter-facing protected evidence blocks.
/app/portfolio-content.ts            @alextsou888-prog

# The verifier and its committed canonical baselines.
/scripts/verify-protected-evidence.mjs   @alextsou888-prog

# Verification wiring (verify:protected / verify scripts).
/package.json                        @alextsou888-prog

# The CI gate itself, including this ownership definition.
/.github/                            @alextsou888-prog
